# Coupled multigroup radiation-hydro fixture for [17c]/#41 (radiation_fld_
# multigroup_equilibration).  Lines beginning with '#' are comments (skipped).
# All numeric tokens are whitespace-delimited and consumed in order.
#
# Layout:
#   ntemp ndens ngroups
#   temps[ntemp]             (eV, log-spaced ascending)
#   densities[ndens]         (g/cc, log-spaced ascending)
#   group_bounds[ngroups+1]  (eV, ascending photon-energy boundaries)
#   planck_absorb[it][id][ig]  (cm^2/g, group index fastest)
#   planck_emiss [it][id][ig]
#   rosseland    [it][id][ig]
#
# Unlike the #24 multigroup_opacity.cn4 fixture (Planck ~1e-4x Rosseland, so
# absorption is optically thin), here the Planck absorption and Rosseland
# transport opacities are COMPARABLE and moderate so the coupled radiation-hydro
# verification (#41) has BOTH a resolvable multigroup diffusion front (Rosseland)
# AND strong matter-radiation coupling (Planck).  Synthetic positive power laws
# (exact under log-log interpolation), reference (rho0,T0) = (1e-2 g/cc, 1e2 eV):
#   rosseland    (ig,rho,T) = KR[ig]*(rho/rho0)^0.6*(T/T0)^-2.0, KR=[3e4,2e4,1.5e4]
#   planck_absorb(ig,rho,T) = KP[ig]*(rho/rho0)^0.6*(T/T0)^-2.0, KP=[5e4,4e4,3e4]
#   planck_emiss = planck_absorb (Kirchhoff).
# At the background (rho0,T0) the extinctions chi_g = rho0*kappa_g are
#   Rosseland {300,200,150} 1/length -> D_g = c/(3 chi_R) = {1.11,1.67,2.22}e-3,
#   Planck    {500,400,300} 1/length -> beta_g = dt c chi_P >> 1 (strong coupling).
# header: ntemp ndens ngroups
         5         4         3
